# Documentation

- EV files in `document/` are the product source of truth. When behavior changes, update BR, Scope, Engineering Spec, Architecture, API, Database, Mapping, and Deployment together.
- Thai-first prose. Keep English model, field, and route names. `document/feature/*` is UI reference only when it matches EV.
- Do not mark a menu done unless EV data, API, and acceptance are met. Separate UI-complete from data-complete.
- Never paste real secrets, tokens, or connection strings. `.env.example` stays placeholders.
- Process commands live in `document/process/db.md` and `docker.md`. Do not revive `package.json` `db:*` or `docker:*` scripts.
- API handbook responses: every JSON field gets a concise Thai comment (what it is and where it comes from).
- New work-item reports under `design/work_items/after_implementation` use Thai-first language with English system terms.
